# Feature 10 — Forgot Password

## Goal
Allow users to reset their password via email if they forget it.

## Flow
1. On the login page, add a "Forgot password?" link below the 
   password input field
2. Clicking it switches to a "Reset password" UI state within 
   the same card (no new page needed)
3. User enters their email address
4. Clicks "Send reset link" button
5. Firebase sends a password reset email to that address
6. Show success message: "Check your email for a reset link."
7. Show a "Back to sign in" link to return to the login form

## UI
- "Forgot password?" link:
  - Placed below the password input, right-aligned
  - Small text, gray color
  - Only visible in sign-in mode (not create account mode)

- Reset password state (replaces the sign-in form):
  - Title: "Reset your password"
  - Subtitle: "Enter your email and we'll send you a reset link."
  - Email input field
  - "Send reset link" button (yellow #FFEA00, #222629 text, full width)
  - "Back to sign in" link below the button, centered, small gray text

- Success state (after sending):
  - Title: "Check your email"
  - Message: "We sent a reset link to [email]. Check your inbox."
  - "Back to sign in" link

- Error state:
  - Show inline error: "No account found with that email."
  - Keep the form visible so user can try again

## Implementation
- Use Firebase Auth: sendPasswordResetEmail(auth, email)
- No new page or route needed — handle as UI state in 
  app/login/page.tsx
- Three states: 'signin' | 'forgot' | 'success'

## Keep Intact
- Animated gradient background
- Floating Arabic letters
- White card styling
- Noto Kufi Arabic logo
- All existing sign-in and create account functionality

